#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detailed Guides: Editing your Document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section of the guide will cover more advanced features of data editing. "
"This section focuses entirely on text data. For working with other types of "
"data, please see the section entitled <link linkend=\"guides-4\">More than "
"just text</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selecting Text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: editing.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid "selecting text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For many editing and formatting functions in &kword;, certain actions (bold "
"face, underline,&etc;) should be applied to a certain section of text, not "
"the document as a whole. You specify which text should be altered by "
"selecting (or highlighting) the text you want changed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selected text has a colored background to separate it from unselected text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select text by designating a start and an end point. All the text in between "
"the start and end point is selected text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Text can be selected with either the <link linkend=\"select-with-mouse"
"\">mouse</link> or the <link linkend=\"select-with-keyboard\">keyboard</"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using The Mouse"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To select text with the mouse, place the mouse pointer at the start point. "
"Click and hold down the &LMB; and drag the mouse pointer. This selects all "
"text between the initial click of &LMB; and the current position of the "
"mouse cursor. When the mouse pointer is at the desired end point, release "
"the button. The start and endpoints will become fixed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using The Keyboard"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To use the keyboard, &kword; takes the initial position of the text cursor "
"as the start point. Use the following key combinations to move the endpoint "
"to the desired location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "Key Combination"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function"
msgstr "Foncion"

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Shift;<keycap>Left Arrow</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moves the endpoint one character to the left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>Left Arrow</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moves the endpoint one word to the left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Shift;<keycap>Right Arrow</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moves the endpoint one character to the Right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>Right Arrow</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moves the endpoint one word to the Right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Shift;<keycap>Up Arrow</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selects all characters from the start of the selection, to the character "
"directly up one line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>Up Arrow</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selects all characters from the start of the selection, to the first "
"character of the line directly above."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Shift;<keycap>Down Arrow</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selects all characters from the start of the selection, to the character "
"directly down one line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>Down Arrow</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selects all characters from the start of the selection, to the last "
"character of the line directly below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Shift;<keycap>Home</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selects all characters from the start of the selection, to the beginning of "
"the line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>Home</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selects all characters from the start of the selection, to the beginning of "
"the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Shift;<keycap>End</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selects all characters from the start of the selection, to the end of the "
"line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>End</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selects all characters from the start of the selection, to the end of the "
"document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Shift;<keycap>Page-Up</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moves the current endpoint one screen up."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>Page-Up</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Moves the current endpoint one page up. The endpoint is located at the first "
"character of this page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Shift;<keycap>Page-Down</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moves the current endpoint down one screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>Page-Down</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Moves the current endpoint down one page. The endpoint is locate at the "
"first character of this page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Ctrl;<keycap>A</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select all text in the current frameset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once the start and endpoints have been defined, all text between the "
"startpoint and endpoint is selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Multiple Views"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: editing.docbook:95 editing.docbook:111 editing.docbook:125
#: editing.docbook:141 editing.docbook:152 editing.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "views"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: editing.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid "using multiple"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When editing very large documents, there will be times when it is helpful to "
"edit two parts of the document. In a situation such as this, &kword; can "
"open additional windows to edit the <emphasis>same</emphasis> document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These new windows are called <emphasis>Views</emphasis>, since they provide "
"a different viewpoint of the the same document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Views are very important tools when working with large documents. Set one "
"view to edit one part of the document, and using the other view, freely move "
"through the document making updates and changes. These changes are "
"automatically revealed in all views."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating a new view"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: editing.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "create new view"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Creating a new view creates an entirely new window, with toolbars, menubars "
"etc. Compare this with the <link linkend=\"views-split\">Split View</link> "
"command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create a new view select <menuchoice><guimenu>View</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>New View</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A new window will be created. Alterations to your document can be made in "
"either view. Updates in one window will be immediately visible in the other."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "Splitting the current view into two separate views."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: editing.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "split current view"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is also possible to split one view into two views. Both views are "
"contained within one window, and use the same toolbars, menubars, etc. "
"Contrast this to the effect of the <link linkend=\"views-new\">New View</"
"link> command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To split the current view, select <menuchoice><guimenu>View</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Split View</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The current document area will be split into two views. Alterations to your "
"document can be made in either view. Updates in one view will be immediately "
"visible in the other."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The views can either be split horizontally or vertically. See the next "
"section for instructions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing the split view orientation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: editing.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "change split view orientation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the direction that the views are split, simply select "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guisubmenu>Splitter Orientation</"
"guisubmenu></menuchoice> from the menubar. This will show a submenu. Select "
"either <guilabel>Horizontal</guilabel> or <guilabel>Vertical</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All views in the current window will immediately change to the new "
"orientation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing the size of views"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: editing.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "resizing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "The relative sizes of each view can be adjusted with your mouse."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To adjust the view size, look at the border between the scrollbar of one "
"view (the upper or right view) and the ruler of the other view (the lower or "
"left view). There is a solid border which appears raised between the "
"scrollbar and the ruler. As the mouse pointer passes over this bar, it "
"changes from an arrow to double lines with double arrows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: editing.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screen shot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the mouse pointer changes, click once with the &LMB; and hold the "
"button down. Drag that border to the new location. When the mouse button is "
"released, the views will change to the new proportions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: editing.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "removing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove a view, simply place the mouse pointer in the view to be deleted "
"and click with the &LMB;. Then select <menuchoice><guimenu>View</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Remove View</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "Close all views"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To close all views, select <indexterm><primary>views</"
"primary><secondary>closing all views</secondary></indexterm> "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Close All Views</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid "Undo/Redo"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: editing.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "undoing last edit"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: editing.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "redoing previously undone edit"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It happens all the time. While working on a document, a change is made. The "
"change was wrong, now you want to back out of your changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fortunately, &kword; has a solution."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each time a change is made to a document, &kword; remembers what the change "
"was. &kword; can <emphasis>Undo</emphasis> each change once a time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As an example, you are writing a business letter and type in the following "
"sentence:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:202 editing.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is a pleasure for me to give you this letter of introduction to your "
"newest employee."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "But that doesn't seem right, so you change it:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is a joy for me to give you this letter of introduction to your newest "
"employee."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid "You decide it was better the first time and you want to change it back."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply select <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Undo</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid "The text now reads <quote>pleasure</quote> again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If, after you Undo a change, and then want to reverse that decision, select "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Redo</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> and the Undo is reversed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sometimes it is not possible for &kword; to undo an edit. In these "
"instances, &kword; will display the <guimenuitem>Undo</guimenuitem> function "
"gray and the function is not accessible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Othertimes, &kword; will only perform a partial undo of the previous task. "
"This is because &kword; processes changes to documents differently then "
"might initially be expected. Simply select <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Undo</guimenuitem></menuchoice> again, and more of the "
"edits will be undone."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, &kword; keeps track of the last 30 edits to the document. This "
"number can be adjusted up or down. For details, see <link linkend=\"opt-misc"
"\">Configuring &kword;</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <emphasis>Undo</emphasis> and <emphasis>Redo</emphasis> commands can be "
"accessed from the menubar (as in the examples above), by using keyboard "
"shortcuts or from the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid "Command"
msgstr "Comanda"

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid "Toolbar Button"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keyboard Shortcut"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid "Undo"
msgstr "Anullar"

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Ctrl;<keycap>Z</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editing.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "Redo"
msgstr "Tornar far"

#. Tag: keycombo
#: editing.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>Z</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cut/Copy/Paste and the Clipboard"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: editing.docbook:257 editing.docbook:303 editing.docbook:341
#: editing.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid "clipboard"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: editing.docbook:257 editing.docbook:1334
#, no-c-format
msgid "using"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>clipboard</quote> is a concept familiar to most people who have "
"used modern word processors. It is a piece of your computers memory which is "
"set aside as a temporary storage space. Text can be <quote>Cut</quote> or "
"<quote>Copied</quote> from your document into the clipboard. You can move to "
"another part of the document or to another application entirely, and "
"<quote>Paste</quote> this text at the new location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The most common use for the clipboard is to move or copy text which has "
"already entered into one part of the document to another part of the same "
"document or to another document entirely."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:271
#, no-c-format
msgid "This concept is probably best described with an example."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid "To do this, we begin with a test sentence"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "The big, red fox jumped over the lazy dog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the mouse or keyboard, select the phrase <quote> big, red</quote> "
"(notice the space before <quote>big</quote> is selected)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Copy</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: editing.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid "This has moved a copy of the selected text to the clipboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now place the mouse cursor directly behind the word <quote>lazy</quote> and "
"click once."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Paste</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:294
#, no-c-format
msgid "The resulting sentence is:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid "The big, red fox jumped over the lazy big, red dog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The clipboard is not limited to text. The clipboard can contain tables, "
"pictures, spreadsheets or any other type of information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenuitem>Copy</guimenuitem> Command"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: editing.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid "copying text to"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:304
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenuitem>Copy</guimenuitem> command can be invoked 4 ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Copy</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"editcopy.png"
"\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the keyboard shortcut: <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>C</"
"keycap></keycombo> or the alternate keyboard shortcut: <keycombo action="
"\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Insert</keycap></keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After the text is selected, click once with the &RMB; and hold the button "
"down. A small popup menu will appear. Simply select <guilabel>Copy</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenuitem>Copy</guimenuitem> command moves a copy of the selected "
"data to the clipboard. <emphasis>The original data is unaffected.</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenuitem>Cut</guimenuitem> Command"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: editing.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid "moving text to"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenuitem>Cut</guimenuitem> command can be invoked 4 ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Cut</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"editcut.png"
"\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the keyboard shortcut: <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>X</"
"keycap></keycombo> or the alternate keyboard shortcut: <keycombo action="
"\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>Delete</keycap></keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After the text is selected, click once with the &RMB; and hold the button "
"down. A small popup menu will appear. Simply select <guilabel>Cut</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenuitem>Cut</guimenuitem> command moves a copy of the selected data "
"to the clipboard. <emphasis>The selected data is then deleted from the "
"document.</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenuitem>Paste</guimenuitem> Command"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: editing.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid "moving text from"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenuitem>Paste</guimenuitem> command can be invoked 4 ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Paste</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"editpaste."
"png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the keyboard shortcut: <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>V</"
"keycap></keycombo> or the alternate keyboard shortcut: <keycombo action="
"\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>Insert</keycap></keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Place the cursor where the contents of the clipboard should be inserted. "
"Click once with the &RMB; and hold the button down. A small popup menu will "
"appear. Simply select <guilabel>Paste</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:407
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenuitem>Paste</guimenuitem> command inserts a copy of all the data "
"in the clipboard at the current position of the cursor. The clipboard is "
"unaffected. (So another paste command will produce yet another copy of the "
"data in the document.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:413
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If no text in the document is currently highlighted, the <guimenuitem>Paste</"
"guimenuitem> command <emphasis>inserts</emphasis> the data at the current "
"position of the cursor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is selected text when the <guimenuitem>Paste</guimenuitem> command "
"is executed, the selected text is <emphasis>replaced</emphasis> with the "
"contents of the clipboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:423
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The clipboard is not limited to the bounds of the current document. If text "
"is copied (or cut) from a document, this text can be pasted into another "
"open document, or another application entirely."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid "Finding and Replacing Text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenuitem>Find</guimenuitem> Command"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: editing.docbook:435
#, no-c-format
msgid "searching for text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: editing.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid "finding text in a document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <quote>Find</quote> command can be invoked 3 ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Find...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the keyboard shortcut:<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;"
"<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:453
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"find.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid "When the Find Command is invoked, a dialog appears."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:468
#, no-c-format
msgid "Basic Text Search"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The combo box labelled <guilabel>Text to find</guilabel>, provides a place "
"for you to enter the text of your search command. (In the screenshot, that "
"box is currently filled with <emphasis>KDE</emphasis>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:474
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you click on <guibutton>Find</guibutton>, then &kword; will search the "
"document until it finds a match to your text. If &kword; cannot find a "
"match, a dialog box will appear that says <guilabel>No matches found for "
"\"Text to find\"</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:478
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to repeat a recent search, simply select the arrow in the drop-"
"down box and a list of your most recent searches will appear. Simply select "
"your search from the list and click <guibutton>Find</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:484 editing.docbook:737
#, no-c-format
msgid "Refining Your Search"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:486 editing.docbook:739
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword;'s find feature is much more sophisticated than we discussed above. "
"Using the options in the dialog box, you can narrow down your search to find "
"<emphasis>exactly</emphasis> what you want."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:492 editing.docbook:745
#, no-c-format
msgid "Regular Expressions in &kword;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:494 editing.docbook:747
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default action for &kword; is to search for an exact match of the text. "
"&kword; has the ability to match text that follows a <emphasis>pattern</"
"emphasis> or a set of rules."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:498 editing.docbook:751
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To enable patterns, place a mark in the box labeled <guilabel>Regular "
"expression</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:500 editing.docbook:753
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will enable the <guibutton>Edit</guibutton> button. This button can be "
"a quick way to create regular expressions for people unfamiliar with &UNIX; "
"regular expressions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:504 editing.docbook:757
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A more thourough discussion of regular expressions in KDE can be found in "
"the help manual for &kregexpeditor;, which can be found in the &khelpcenter;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:508 editing.docbook:761
#, no-c-format
msgid "Formatting options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:509 editing.docbook:762
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; also has the ability to search your document for text that matches "
"certain formatting options as well as the text itself."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:512 editing.docbook:765
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To include formatting options in your search, click the button labeled "
"<guibutton>Show Formatting Options</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:515 editing.docbook:768 editing.docbook:952
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once <guibutton>Show Formatting Options</guibutton> has been clicked, a new "
"dialog will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:524 editing.docbook:777
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use this dialog to select the options you want to include in your "
"search."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:525 editing.docbook:778
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The left column consists of 13 check boxes. If there is a mark in the check "
"box, then &kword; will evaluate any searchable text for that property. If no "
"mark is in the check box, &kword; does not consider that property when "
"performing a search."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:531 editing.docbook:784 editing.docbook:969
#: editing.docbook:1605
#, no-c-format
msgid "Family:"
msgstr "Familha :"

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:533 editing.docbook:786
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this combo box to select the font family you want to include in your "
"search text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:538 editing.docbook:791 editing.docbook:976
#: editing.docbook:1612
#, no-c-format
msgid "Size:"
msgstr "Talha :"

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:540 editing.docbook:793
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use this spin box to set the font size you want &kword; to search for."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: editing.docbook:545 editing.docbook:798 editing.docbook:983
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Color:</guilabel> and <guilabel>Background color:</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:547 editing.docbook:800
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking on either of these two buttons allows you to select the font color "
"and/or background color respectively, you want &kword; to search for. For "
"more information on selecting a color, see the section on <link linkend="
"\"select-colors\">Selecting Colors from the Color Dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: editing.docbook:555 editing.docbook:808 editing.docbook:992
#: editing.docbook:1628
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Bold:</guilabel> and <guilabel>Italic:</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:557 editing.docbook:810
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use these <guilabel>Yes</guilabel>/<guilabel>No</guilabel> radio boxes to "
"determine whether you want &kword; to include boldface or italicized fonts "
"in the search text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:563 editing.docbook:816 editing.docbook:1000
#: editing.docbook:1636
#, no-c-format
msgid "Strikeout:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:565 editing.docbook:818
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select <guilabel>None</guilabel>, <guilabel>Single</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Double</guilabel> or <guilabel>Simple Bold</guilabel> to modify "
"your search."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:571 editing.docbook:824 editing.docbook:1008
#, no-c-format
msgid "Underline:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:573 editing.docbook:826
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select <guilabel>None</guilabel>, <guilabel>Single</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Double</guilabel>, <guilabel>Simple Bold</guilabel> or "
"<guilabel>Wave</guilabel> to modify your search."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:579 editing.docbook:832 editing.docbook:1016
#: editing.docbook:1652
#, no-c-format
msgid "Vertical alignment:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:581 editing.docbook:834
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select <guilabel>Normal</guilabel>, <guilabel>Subscript</guilabel> "
"or <guilabel>Superscript</guilabel> to determine what font alignment you "
"want &kword; to search for."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: editing.docbook:587 editing.docbook:840 editing.docbook:1023
#: editing.docbook:1659
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Shadow:</guilabel> and <guilabel>Word by word:</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:589 editing.docbook:842
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use these <guilabel>Yes</guilabel>/<guilabel>No</guilabel> radio boxes to "
"determine whether you want &kword; to include shadow text in the search text "
"and whether to search for word by word underlining and strikethrough text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:595 editing.docbook:848 editing.docbook:1031
#: editing.docbook:1667
#, no-c-format
msgid "Capitalization:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:597 editing.docbook:850
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select <guilabel>Normal</guilabel>, <guilabel>Uppercase</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Lowercase</guilabel>, or <guilabel>Small Caps</guilabel> to "
"determine what capitalization you want &kword; to search for."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:603 editing.docbook:856 editing.docbook:1039
#: editing.docbook:1675
#, no-c-format
msgid "Language:"
msgstr "Lenga :"

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:605 editing.docbook:858
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select the language of the text you want &kword; to search for using "
"this dropdown box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:609 editing.docbook:862 editing.docbook:939
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have selected your options, click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to "
"accept your search options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:610 editing.docbook:863 editing.docbook:940
#: editing.docbook:1047 editing.docbook:1683
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> to ignore all changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:611 editing.docbook:864 editing.docbook:941
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>Reset</guibutton> to restore the options dialog box to the "
"default values."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:612 editing.docbook:865 editing.docbook:942
#: editing.docbook:1049 editing.docbook:1685
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>Clear</guibutton> to remove all marks from the checked "
"options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:617 editing.docbook:870
#, no-c-format
msgid "Other Search options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:619 editing.docbook:872
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In addition to pattern matching, you can limit the search results with a few "
"useful options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:624 editing.docbook:877 editing.docbook:1081
#, no-c-format
msgid "Case sensitive"
msgstr "Respectar la cassa"

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:626 editing.docbook:879 editing.docbook:1083
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When this option is selected, &kword; will not only search for the string of "
"letters, but will verify that the case of the letters is the same. For "
"example. Searching for: <emphasis>KDE</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:629 editing.docbook:882
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"will match: <emphasis>KDE</emphasis> and <emphasis>hiddenKDEinwords</"
"emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:631 editing.docbook:884
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"but not: <emphasis>Kde, kde</emphasis> or <emphasis> hiddenkdeinwords</"
"emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:637 editing.docbook:890 editing.docbook:1094
#, no-c-format
msgid "Find backwards"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:639 editing.docbook:892 editing.docbook:1096
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option changes the direction of the search. This can be useful when you "
"only want to search for a string of text before the current cursor position, "
"not after. This option is usually used in conjunction with <guilabel>From "
"cursor</guilabel>, but if that option is not specified, &kword; will start "
"searching from the end of the document backwards."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:649 editing.docbook:902 editing.docbook:1106
#, no-c-format
msgid "Whole words only"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:651 editing.docbook:904 editing.docbook:1108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When this option is selected, &kword; will only return search items that are "
"surrounded by spaces, paragraph marks or punctuation. For example. Searching "
"for: <emphasis>KDE</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:653 editing.docbook:906 editing.docbook:1110
#, no-c-format
msgid "will match: <emphasis>KDE</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:654 editing.docbook:907 editing.docbook:1111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"but not: <emphasis> hiddenKDEinwords</emphasis> or <emphasis>KDElike</"
"emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:660 editing.docbook:913 editing.docbook:1117
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selected Text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:661 editing.docbook:914 editing.docbook:1118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to limit your search to a specific part of the document (a few "
"paragraphs, for example), you can select the part of the document you want "
"to search <emphasis>prior</emphasis> to selecting the <guilabel>Find</"
"guilabel> command. When text is selected, &kword; will default to only "
"searching the selected text. You can use this option to enable or disable "
"this restriction."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:668 editing.docbook:921 editing.docbook:1126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option will not be available if you have not selected text prior to "
"selecting the <guilabel>Find</guilabel> command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:675 editing.docbook:928 editing.docbook:1133
#, no-c-format
msgid "From cursor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:677 editing.docbook:930 editing.docbook:1135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, &kword; begins searching at the beginning of the document. If "
"this option is selected, &kword; begins its search from the current position "
"of the cursor. The direction that &kword; searches is, by default forward in "
"the document, but can be changed with the <guilabel>Find backwards</"
"guilabel> option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:690
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenuitem>Replace</guimenuitem> Command"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:692
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenuitem>Replace</guimenuitem> command is an extension of the "
"<guimenuitem>Find</guimenuitem> command. If you are familiar with the "
"<guimenuitem>Find</guimenuitem> command, you will see many similarities."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:696
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Replace</guilabel> command can be invoked 2 ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:701
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Replace...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:707
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the keyboard shortcut: <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;"
"<keycap>R</keycap></keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:712
#, no-c-format
msgid "When the <guilabel>Replace</guilabel> command is invoked, a dialog appears."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:721
#, no-c-format
msgid "Basic Search and Replace"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: editing.docbook:722
#, no-c-format
msgid "replacing text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:724
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The combo box labeled <guilabel>Text to find:</guilabel>, provides a place "
"for you to enter the text of your search command. (In the screenshot, that "
"box is currently filled with <emphasis>KDE</emphasis>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:729
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can enter your replacement text in the text box labeled "
"<guilabel>Replacement text:</guilabel>. You can now click <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton> to replace all occurrences in the document, or you can further "
"refine your search."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:946
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replace with formatted text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:947
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; also has the ability to replace the found text with formatted text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:949
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To include formatting options in your search, click the button labeled "
"<guibutton>Show Formatting Options</guibutton> in the <guilabel>Replace "
"With</guilabel> section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:961 editing.docbook:1597
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can use this dialog to select the format of the replaced text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:962 editing.docbook:1598
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The left column consists of 13 check boxes. If there is a mark in the check "
"box, then &kword; will change any replaced text to match the property "
"selected. If no mark is in the check box, &kword; does not consider that "
"property when replacing text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:971 editing.docbook:1607
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this combo box to select the font family you want your replacement text "
"to use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:978 editing.docbook:1614
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this spin box to set the font size you want &kword; to use for your "
"replaced text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:985 editing.docbook:1621
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking on either of these two buttons allows you to select the font color "
"and/or background color respectively, you want &kword; to use. For more "
"information on selecting a color, see the section on <link linkend=\"select-"
"colors\">Selecting Colors from the Color Dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:994 editing.docbook:1630
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use these <guilabel>Yes</guilabel>/<guilabel>No</guilabel> radio boxes to "
"determine whether you want &kword; to change the fonts to boldface or "
"italicized fonts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1002 editing.docbook:1638
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select <guilabel>None</guilabel>, <guilabel>Single</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Double</guilabel> or <guilabel>Simple Bold</guilabel> to use for "
"the replacement text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1010 editing.docbook:1646
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select <guilabel>None</guilabel>, <guilabel>Single</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Double</guilabel>, <guilabel>Simple Bold</guilabel> or "
"<guilabel>Wave</guilabel> to use for the replacement text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1018 editing.docbook:1654
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select <guilabel>Normal</guilabel>, <guilabel>Subscript</guilabel> "
"or <guilabel>Superscript</guilabel> to determine what font alignment you "
"want &kword; to use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1025 editing.docbook:1661
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use these <guilabel>Yes</guilabel>/<guilabel>No</guilabel> radio boxes to "
"determine whether you want &kword; to use shadow text and/or word by word "
"underlining and strikethrough in the replacement text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1033 editing.docbook:1669
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select <guilabel>Normal</guilabel>, <guilabel>Uppercase</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Lowercase</guilabel>, or <guilabel>Small Caps</guilabel> to "
"determine what capitalization to use for the replacement text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1041 editing.docbook:1677
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select the language of the text you will use to replace the found "
"text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1046 editing.docbook:1682
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have selected your options, click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to "
"accept your text options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1048 editing.docbook:1684
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>Reset</guibutton> to restore the options dialog box to the "
"initial values prior to making any changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1053
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using placeholders"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1054
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Placeholders are useful when you want to add text to complex search strings. "
"Currently &kword; has only one placeholder: <emphasis>Complete text string</"
"emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1056
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This placeholder will contain the entire text string matched by the "
"<guimenuitem>Find</guimenuitem> command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1057
#, no-c-format
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1058
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You create a search string, using regular expressions: <emphasis>Reference "
"\\d</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1059
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order for this string example to work, a mark must be placed in the check "
"box labeled <guilabel>Regular expression</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1061
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Regular expressions are available by placing a mark in this checkbox. The "
"use of regular expressions is beyond the scope of this manual. For more "
"information see the KDE Regular Expression Manual (Available in the &kde; "
"help center)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1063
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now in the <guilabel>Replace With</guilabel> section of the replace dialog, "
"you place a mark in the check box labeled <guilabel>Use placeholders</"
"guilabel>. Click the <guibutton>Insert Placeholder</guibutton> button and "
"select <guilabel>Complete Match</guilabel>. &kword; will insert a <emphasis>"
"\\0</emphasis> in the <guilabel>Replacement text:</guilabel> text box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1067
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now surround the placeholder with parentheses, so your text string is: "
"<emphasis>(\\0)</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1068
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When this is executed, whenever &kword; encounters the find text (ie. "
"<quote>Reference 0</quote>, <quote>Reference 1</quote>, <quote>Reference 2</"
"quote>, etc) it will surround the text in parenthesis (<quote>(Reference 0)</"
"quote>, <quote>(Reference 1)</quote>, <quote>(Reference 2)</quote>, "
"respectively)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1071
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As you can see, the placeholder will maintain a copy of the search text. You "
"can use this placeholder to add text to the ends of any search string you "
"can imagine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1076
#, no-c-format
msgid "Other Replace Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1078
#, no-c-format
msgid "Additional options in the dialog are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1086
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"will match: <emphasis>KDE</emphasis> and <emphasis>hiddenKDEinwords</"
"emphasis> but not: <emphasis>Kde, kde</emphasis> or <emphasis> "
"hiddenkdeinwords</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1144
#, no-c-format
msgid "Prompt on replace"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1146
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, &kword; will prompt the user <emphasis>before</"
"emphasis> each replacement. This allows you to approve or disapprove each "
"replacement."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1162
#, no-c-format
msgid "Spellchecking"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: editing.docbook:1163 editing.docbook:1287
#, no-c-format
msgid "spelling"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: editing.docbook:1163
#, no-c-format
msgid "check spelling of document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; can compare each word in your document to several commonly available "
"dictionaries. It will offer you the opportunity to change any words it "
"believes are misspelled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, if any text in the document is selected, &kword; only checks the "
"spelling of currently selected text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to check the spelling of a specific part of your document, "
"simply <link linkend=\"select\">select the text</link> you want to check the "
"spelling of."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1171
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To check the entire document, leave all text in the document unsellected, "
"and &kword; will check the entire document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1173
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can check the spelling of text 2 ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guisubmenu>Spellcheck</"
"guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Spelling...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the "
"menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"spell.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1189
#, no-c-format
msgid "Spellchecking your document is controlled through a dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this example, the misspelled word &kword; found, was <emphasis>youve</"
"emphasis>. The currently suggested replacement word is listed in the text "
"box labeled <guilabel>Replace with:</guilabel>. In the list box labeled "
"<guilabel>Suggested Words</guilabel> is a list of words the spelling program "
"has determined as possible correct spellings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1204
#, no-c-format
msgid "From here you have eight options:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: editing.docbook:1208
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replace"
msgstr "Remplaçar"

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1210
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Replaces the current word with the suggested word. Only replaces this "
"occurrence."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: editing.docbook:1216
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replace All"
msgstr "Tot remplaçar"

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Replaces all occurrences of the current word with the suggested word through "
"the entire document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: editing.docbook:1224
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ignore"
msgstr "Ignorar"

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Do not make any changes to this occurrence. Ask again if this word appears "
"further down in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: editing.docbook:1232
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ignore All"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1234
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Do not make any changes to this or any other occurrence of this word. Do not "
"ask about this word again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: editing.docbook:1240
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Add</guibutton>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1242
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add the current word to the dictionary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: editing.docbook:1247
#, no-c-format
msgid "Stop"
msgstr "Arrêter"

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1249
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keep the current changes, but stop any further checking."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: editing.docbook:1254
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cancel"
msgstr "Anullar"

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1256
#, no-c-format
msgid "Stop spellchecking."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: editing.docbook:1261
#, no-c-format
msgid "Help"
msgstr "Ajuda"

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1263
#, no-c-format
msgid "Loads a help file for the spellchecker."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1268
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the entire document has been checked, &kword; will return the cursor to "
"the same spot in the document that the spellchecking was begun."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1272
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the document does not have any spelling errors, &kword; does not show a "
"dialog box informing you there were no spelling errors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1275
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When spellchecking is started, it will proceed to check all of the document "
"against the dictionary, and if there are no spelling errors it will close "
"the spellcheck dialog box. With short documents, this may happen quickly. "
"&kword; has spellchecked the document!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1281
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are several options for configuring the spelling application used. For "
"more details, please see the section entitled <link linkend=\"opt-spell"
"\">Configure Spelling</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1286
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatically mark misspelled words"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: editing.docbook:1287
#, no-c-format
msgid "automatically mark misspelled words"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1289
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; can check the spelling of your document as you edit it. It will "
"underline in red any word which it cannot find in the dictionary. This "
"behavior can be turned on and off by the user. By selecting <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guisubmenu>Spellcheck</"
"guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Autospellcheck</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the "
"menubar you can toggle autospellchecking on and off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1298
#, no-c-format
msgid "Finding related word (Thesaurus)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: editing.docbook:1299
#, no-c-format
msgid "thesaurus, using"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: editing.docbook:1300
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wordnet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: editing.docbook:1301
#, no-c-format
msgid "related words"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1303
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; comes with a small thesaurus based on the Wordnet project. For more "
"information on Wordnet, visit the <ulink url=\"http://www.cogsci.princeton."
"edu/~wn/\">Wordnet homepage</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1305
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can invoke the thesaurus two ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1308
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply click on the desired word with the &RMB;. A popup menu will appear. "
"Select <guimenuitem>Show Related Words</guimenuitem> from the menu and a "
"dialog will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1310
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Related "
"Words</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1315
#, no-c-format
msgid "Which ever method you choose, &kword; opens the &kthesaurus; dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1321
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The word you selected from your document appears in the combo box labeled "
"<guilabel>Search for:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1322
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are three columns of alternate words: <guilabel>Synonyms</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>More General words</guilabel> (hypernyms), <guilabel>More Specific "
"Words</guilabel> (hyponyms)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you find an appropriate alternate word, simply click on the word in the "
"list, and this word will now be listed in the text box labeled "
"<guilabel>Replace With:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1325
#, no-c-format
msgid "To finalize the replacement click <guibutton>Replace</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1326
#, no-c-format
msgid "To keep your original word, click <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1327
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To obtain more specific help, or for help on using the full version of "
"Wordnet, click the <guibutton>Help</guibutton> button for help with "
"&kthesaurus; (including additional thesauri for non-english languages)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1333
#, no-c-format
msgid "Autocorrection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: editing.docbook:1334 editing.docbook:1359 editing.docbook:1691
#: editing.docbook:1730
#, no-c-format
msgid "autocorrection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1336
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Auto correction is a system for correcting common typing errors, converting "
"abbreviations to their full spelling and adjusting capitalization. As you "
"could guess from its name, this all occurs automatically, while you are "
"editing your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1342
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enabling/Disabling Autocorrection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1344
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To toggle autocorrection on, select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu><guisubmenu>Autocorrection</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Enable "
"Autocorrection</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. When enabled, "
"autocorrection makes changes to your document <emphasis>as you type</"
"emphasis>. You can determine which changes to make by <link linkend="
"\"configure-autocorrection\">configuring autocorrection</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1350
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To toggle autocorrection off, select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu><guisubmenu>Autocorrection</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Disable "
"Autocorrection</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. When disabled, "
"autocorrection changes are not made. You can, however, <link linkend="
"\"autoformat\">apply autocorrection manually</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1358
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring Autocorrection Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: editing.docbook:1359
#, no-c-format
msgid "configuring"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1361
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To adjust the options for autocorrection, select <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Autocorrection...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1365
#, no-c-format
msgid "A dialog window appears to help you set your options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1368
#, no-c-format
msgid "Simple Autocorrection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1380
#, no-c-format
msgid "Convert first letter of a sentence automatically to uppercase"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1383
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When selected, &kword; will automatically capitalize the first letter after "
"a period. You can tell &kword; when not to alter capitalization in certain "
"instances (ie <quote>Sr.</quote> or <quote>Jr.</quote>. For more details, "
"see the section entitled <link linkend=\"autocorrection-exceptions"
"\">Autocorrection Exceptions</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1391
#, no-c-format
msgid "Convert two uppercase letters to one uppercase and one lowercase letter"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When selected, &kword; will automatically convert a double capital letter (a "
"common typographical error), into a single capital letter. You can tell "
"&kword; when not to alter capitalization in certain instances. For more "
"details, see the section entitled <link linkend=\"autocorrection-exceptions"
"\">Autocorrection Exceptions</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1403
#, no-c-format
msgid "Autoformat URLs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1405
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When selected, &kword; will scan text for patterns which suggest a certain "
"section of text is a <glossterm linkend=\"defurl\">URL</glossterm> and "
"automatically creates a link."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1407
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more details on links, see the section entitled <link linkend=\"links"
"\">Document Links</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1413
#, no-c-format
msgid "Suppress double spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1415
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, &kword; will ignore the second space typed. This prevents "
"users from adding double spaces between words or sentences"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1421
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove spaces at the beginning and end of paragraphs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1423
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When selected, &kword; will automatically remove spaces at the beginning and/"
"or the end of a line of text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1428
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatically do bold and underline formatting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1430
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When selected, &kword; will look for words surrounded by asterisks ( * ). It "
"will remove the asterisks and change the font of all words in between the "
"two asterisks to bold face."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1432
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; will also look for words surrounded by underscores ( _ ). It will "
"remove the underscores and underline all words in between the two "
"underscores."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1438
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replace 1/2... with ½..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1440
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When selected, &kword; will automatically change 1/2, 1/3 and 3/4 to their "
"single character equivalents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1445
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use autonumbering for numbered paragraphs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1447
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you start a paragraph with a number and a symbol (<emphasis> 1) </"
"emphasis> for example). &kword; will automatically convert that paragraph to "
"a numbered paragraph. All future paragraphs will be consecutively numbered."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1453
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replace 1st with 1^st"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1455
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When selected, &kword; will automatically change 1st to 1<superscript>st</"
"superscript>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1460
#, no-c-format
msgid "Capitalize name of days"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1462
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Automatically capitalize the days of the week (Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, "
"etc...)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1467
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use list-formatting for bulleted paragraphs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1469
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When selected, &kword; will look for lines that begin with <emphasis>- </"
"emphasis>, and automatically convert the paragraph style to a bulleted list. "
"The bullet is selected with the left button below this option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1478
#, no-c-format
msgid "Custom Quotes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1479
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select the tab labeled <guilabel>Custom Quotes</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1489
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replace double quotes with typographical quotes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1491
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When selected, this option will replace the standard keyboard double quotes, "
"with typographical quotation marks. If you want to change the quotation "
"character, click on one of the buttons. Clicking on <guibutton>Default</"
"guibutton>, restores the default paragraph marks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1499
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replace single quotes with typographical quotes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1501
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When selected, this option will replace the standard keyboard single quotes, "
"with typographical quotation marks. If you want to change the quotation "
"character, click on one of the buttons. Clicking on <guibutton>Default</"
"guibutton>, restores the default paragraph marks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1510
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced Autocorrection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1512
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To switch to the Advanced Autocorrection, click on the tab labeled "
"<guilabel>Advanced Autocorrection</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1519
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This allows you to automatically have &kword; replace one string of text "
"with another. This can be useful for special symbols, commonly used "
"abbreviations that you want spelled out, or abbreviations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1523
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; uses different autocorrection strings depending on the language. Set "
"the correct language using the combo box labeled <guilabel>Replacements and "
"exceptions for language:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1527
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The check box labeled <guilabel>Enable word replacement</guilabel> is used "
"to toggle on and off the autoreplacement features of &kword;. If there is no "
"mark in the check box, then &kword; will not perform any autoreplacements "
"from the list in this dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1531
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is a mark in the check box labeled <guilabel>Replace text with "
"format</guilabel> &kword; will not only change the text when it finds a "
"match, but it will change the formatting of the new text. If there is no "
"mark in this check box, then &kword; uses the same formatting options for "
"the replaced text as it found in the search text. For more information on "
"setting the format options for replacement text, see the section on <link "
"linkend=\"autocorrection-format-options\">Changing the format of the "
"autocorrection string</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1539
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding an autocorrection string"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1541
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add an autocorrection string, simply type the text you want &kword; to "
"check for in the text box labeled <guilabel>Find</guilabel>, then enter the "
"text you want &kword; to substitute in the text box labeled "
"<guilabel>Replace</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1547
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to insert symbols or special characters not available on your "
"keyboard, you can click the buttons with three periods on them and select a "
"special character from the table provided."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1551
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When these are entered, click <guibutton>Add</guibutton>. Your text strings "
"are now added to the table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1556
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editing an autocorrection string"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: editing.docbook:1557
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing the text you want to find."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1558
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; does not allow you to change the text to search for. This is to "
"prevent disastrous mistakes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1560
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Instead, you must delete the current autocorrection rule and add a new text "
"string with the corrected text to find."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: editing.docbook:1563
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing the text you want to replace."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1564
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Begin by clicking once on the string you want to edit. It will be "
"highlighted and the find and replace text will be listed in the text boxes "
"above. You can alter the replacement text. When you are done, simply select "
"<guibutton>Modify</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1572
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deleting an autocorrection string."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1574
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply click on the string you want to delete. Now click the "
"<guibutton>Remove</guibutton> button. The string is removed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1578
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Be aware that &kword; does not give you a chance to back out once you have "
"deleted a string. Be sure you have selected the correct string "
"<emphasis>before</emphasis> you click the <guibutton>Remove</guibutton> "
"button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1586
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing the format of the autocorrection string."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1587
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Currently, you must create the autocorrection string <emphasis>before</"
"emphasis> you can format it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1588
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once the autocorrection string has been created, simply click on it once "
"with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1589
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now click on the <guibutton>Change Format...</guibutton> button. A small "
"dialog will appear:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: editing.docbook:1619
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Color:</guilabel> and <guilabel>Background Color:</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1644
#, no-c-format
msgid "Underline"
msgstr "Soslinhat"

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1690
#, no-c-format
msgid "Autocorrection Exceptions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: editing.docbook:1692
#, no-c-format
msgid "exceptions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1694
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are instances where &kword; will make autocorrection changes that are "
"inappropriate. You can use the fourth tab of this dialog to define "
"<emphasis>exceptions</emphasis> to the rules previously discussed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1697
#, no-c-format
msgid "The dialog for exceptions is shown below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1703
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To prevent &kword; from deciding an abbreviation or other text is the end of "
"a sentence, simply enter the text fragment in the text box below "
"<guilabel>Do not treat as the end of a sentence:</guilabel>. Then click "
"<guibutton>Add</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1707
#, no-c-format
msgid "As an example: Adding <quote>Jr.</quote> to this dialog prevents"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: quote
#: editing.docbook:1708
#, no-c-format
msgid "Robert Jones Jr. is a friend of the family."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1709 editing.docbook:1721
#, no-c-format
msgid "from being changed to:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: quote
#: editing.docbook:1710
#, no-c-format
msgid "Robert Jones Jr. Is a friend of the family."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1711 editing.docbook:1723
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove an erroneous entry, simply click once on the wrong entry with the "
"&LMB; and click on the <guibutton>Remove</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1713
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The second set of boxes performs a similar function to the first except text "
"entered in these boxes will allow two capital letters in a word if it is "
"entered in this text box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1716
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply enter the word in the text box below <guilabel>Accept two uppercase "
"letters in:</guilabel>. Then click <guibutton>Add</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1719
#, no-c-format
msgid "As an example: Adding <quote>CD</quote> to this dialog prevents"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: quote
#: editing.docbook:1720
#, no-c-format
msgid "<quote>CD</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: quote
#: editing.docbook:1722
#, no-c-format
msgid "<quote>Cd</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1729
#, no-c-format
msgid "Manually applying autocorrection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: editing.docbook:1730
#, no-c-format
msgid "manually applying"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1733
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If autocorrection is turned off in your document, you can manually enable "
"<link linkend=\"autocorrect\">autocorrection</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1734
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To manually apply autocorrection, first configure your options by using the "
"<link linkend=\"configure-autocorrection\">autocorrection dialogs</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1736
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guisubmenu>Autocorrection</"
"guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Apply Autocorrection</guimenuitem></menuchoice> "
"from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1740
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; will start at the beginning of the document and apply all selected "
"autocorrection options to the entire document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1742
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When &kword; is finished, it will return you to your document for further "
"editing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1743
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on enabling and disabling autocorrection, see <link "
"linkend=\"autocorrection-enable\">Enabling/Disabling Autocorrection</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1750
#, no-c-format
msgid "Autocompletion"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: editing.docbook:1751
#, no-c-format
msgid "autocompletion"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1753
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Autocompletion allows you to type the first few letters of a commonly used "
"word (often technical or job specific), and tell &kword; to finish typing "
"the word for you. This is often very useful when you have lengthy technical "
"words."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1758
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using autocompletion"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1759
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using autocompletion could not be easier. Simply type the first few letters "
"of the word you want &kword; to finish, and press <keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>E</"
"keycap></keycombo>. &kword; will look through the list of autocompletion "
"words and if it finds a word which begins with those letters, it will finish "
"entering the remainder of the word."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1765
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding words to autocompletion"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1766
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; maintains a list of words for each user that will be used for "
"autocompletion."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1768
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can add words to this list one of two ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1770
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; can automatically add new words to the completion list for later "
"approval. This is selected using <link linkend=\"autocomplete-dialog\">the "
"dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1774
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Individual words can be added to the list by using <link linkend="
"\"autocomplete-dialog\">the dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editing.docbook:1780
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring autocomplete"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1781
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To configure autocompletion, select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Completion...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from "
"the menubar. This will bring up a dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1795
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable word completion"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1796
#, no-c-format
msgid "It is used to toggle autocompletion on and off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1800
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Add</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1802
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By clicking this button you can manually add an individual word to the "
"completion list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1808
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove"
msgstr "Suprimir"

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1810
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove words from the completion list, select the word with the &LMB; "
"from the list, then click this button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1816
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatically add new words to suggestion list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1818
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option will add any word equal to or longer than the "
"<guilabel>Characters needed:</guilabel> to the list of proposed "
"autocompletion words."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1821
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The large listbox in the center of the dialog contains the current proposed "
"list of autocompletion words."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1823
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Not all words listed in the list box will be immediatly affected by "
"autocompletion when entered into this dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1829
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show words in tooltip"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1831
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, a tool tip box will appear when you type the "
"beginning of a word that exists in the completion list. To complete the "
"word, press the key you set to accept suggestions in the <guilabel>Key to "
"accept suggestion:</guilabel> drop-down list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1840
#, no-c-format
msgid "Characters needed:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1842
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this spinbox/slider combination to prevent &kword; from automatically "
"adding short words to the completion list. You can select any value from 5-"
"100 and the words will need to be at least the number of characters set here "
"to be added in the list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1850
#, no-c-format
msgid "Suggest words:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1852
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This spinbox/slider combination can be adjusted to allow more or less words "
"into the autocompletion list. This option is most important when "
"<guilabel>Automatically add new words to suggestion list</guilabel> is "
"enabled. This option keeps the list from becoming too cumbersome. You can "
"select any value from 1 to 500."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1861
#, no-c-format
msgid "Append space"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1863
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If checked, it adds a single space to the end of a word after "
"autocompletion, this means it is not necessary to add the space manually for "
"the next word."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1870
#, no-c-format
msgid "Key to accept suggestion:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1872
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set the key you want to use when an autocompleted word is suggested to you "
"and you want to accept it. You can choose <keycap>Enter</keycap>, "
"<keycap>Tab</keycap>, <keycap>Space</keycap>, <keycap>End</keycap> or "
"<keycap>Right</keycap>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: editing.docbook:1880
#, no-c-format
msgid "Make Default"
msgstr "Valeurs par défaut"

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1882
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A word is not part of autocompletion until the list is <emphasis>saved</"
"emphasis> to disk. At that moment, &kword; will use that saved list for all "
"autocompletion, until the list is replaced with another saved list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1886
#, no-c-format
msgid "Some of the words in the autocompletion list may not have been saved yet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1887
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To save the current list to disk and have &kword; begin using this new list "
"for autocompletion, click this button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editing.docbook:1894
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to save your options. Click "
"<guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> to abort all changes. Click <guibutton>Reset</"
"guibutton> to reset to the state after you clicked on the <guibutton>Make "
"Default</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

